---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import WorkDossier from "../components/WorkDossier.astro";
import { projects } from "../data/projects";
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import avatar from "../assets/avatar.png";
import "../styles/sketch.css";
---

<Layout
  title="Portfolio | Sketch"
  description="A single-page portfolio focused on practical agent workflows, long-running automation systems, and careful execution."
>
  <main class="page-shell">
    <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-heading">
      <p class="hero-kicker">Hi, I am Zhou Le.</p>
      <h1 id="hero-heading">I build agent workflows that already run outside the demo.</h1>
      <p class="hero-lead">
        This site is a small record of systems I have built while learning AI tooling, coding
        agents, and workflow automation through practice.
      </p>
      <p class="hero-supporting">
        I am still early in this work, but I care most about systems that keep their state,
        recover context, and stay useful after the first successful run.
      </p>
      <p class="status-line">
        <span class="status-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        A small record of real work, not a personal brand exercise.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="about-bridge" aria-labelledby="about-heading">
      <div class="about-bridge-grid">
        <div class="profile-card">
          <div class="profile-card-frame">
            <Image
              class="profile-card-avatar"
              src={avatar}
              alt="Portrait of Zhou Le"
              width={144}
              height={144}
              loading="lazy"
            />
          </div>
          <div class="profile-card-copy">
            <p class="profile-card-name">Zhou Le</p>
            <dl class="profile-card-facts">
              <div class="profile-card-fact">
                <dt>Focus</dt>
                <dd>Agent workflows</dd>
              </div>
              <div class="profile-card-fact">
                <dt>Background</dt>
                <dd>B.Eng. in Software Engineering; M.A. in Translation</dd>
              </div>
              <div class="profile-card-fact">
                <dt>Tools</dt>
                <dd>Codex, Opencode, OpenClaw</dd>
              </div>
              <div class="profile-card-fact">
                <dt>GitHub</dt>
                <dd>
                  <a
                    class="profile-card-link"
                    href="https://github.com/fancydirty"
                    target="_blank"
                    rel="noreferrer"
                  >
                    fancydirty
                  </a>
                </dd>
              </div>
            </dl>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="about-bridge-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">About Me</p>
        <h2 id="about-heading">I came to systems work through language, and I am learning it by building.</h2>
        <p>
          I hold a master's degree in translation from UESTC. Before I started building agent
          workflows, I spent years working with language and content. That background made me care
          about precision, structure, and whether something still makes sense once another person
          has to pick it up.
        </p>
        <p>
          Over the last year, I have turned that same habit toward AI tooling, coding agents, and
          workflow automation. I learn by building systems that need to keep running, seeing where
          they drift, and then tightening the state, checks, and guardrails until they behave
          better. Codex, Opencode, and OpenClaw are the tools I return to most. The projects below
          are the clearest record of that shift so far.
        </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <WorkDossier projects={projects} />

    <section class="lower-grid">
      <section class="manifesto" aria-labelledby="principles-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">How I Work</p>
        <h2 id="principles-heading">A few principles I keep returning to.</h2>
        <ul class="principles-list">
          <li>Evidence before action.</li>
          <li>Verification after side effects.</li>
          <li>State over guesswork.</li>
          <li>Bootstrap and guardrails matter.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="now-panel" aria-labelledby="now-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">Now</p>
        <h2 id="now-heading">Focused on workflows that behave well over time.</h2>
        <p>
          Right now I am most interested in long-running automation, practical agent discipline,
          and making AI systems feel less theatrical and more dependable.
        </p>
        <p>
          These projects are not mass-market products, and that is okay. What interests me right
          now is how agents lower the cost of building software around a specific person, team, or
          workflow. That makes a different kind of project feel possible: not just software that
          tries to fit everyone, but systems that can be shaped more closely to a real context and
          then made reliable enough to keep running. That is the direction I want to keep learning
          in.
        </p>

        <ul class="links-list" aria-label="links">
          <li>
            <a href="https://github.com/fancydirty" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">GitHub</a>
          </li>
          <li>
            <a href="https://github.com/fancydirty/clawd-media-track" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
              clawd-media-track
            </a>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>
    </section>

    <footer class="site-footer">
      <p>
        This site is intentionally small. The goal is to show real systems, modestly and
        clearly.
      </p>
    </footer>
  </main>
</Layout>
